  message: "Done (PR auto-merged to dev). Added metrics.by_supply_chain_tier.{tier}.edges_incident (either-endpoint count) alongside the existing source-tier 'edges'. The existing 'edges' is source-tier so external-dep tiers (2/3) — graph sinks — read ~0; edges_incident exposes their real contribution (counts each edge once per distinct resolved endpoint tier). Double-counts cross-tier edges by design; does NOT sum to total_edges (source-tier 'edges' remains the reconciling view, summing to the source-resolved total). Spec section metrics updated; INV-jukok preserved (unresolved endpoints skipped). Behavioral evidence: test_metrics.py::test_by_tier_edges_src_vs_edges_incident — a tier-1->tier-3 sink graph yields external_dep edges=0 but edges_incident=2 (was: only 0 visible). Full affected suite 2767 passed, metrics.py 100%."  # 13a7
